  "configuration_id": "config_031",
  "reason": "Evidence: The current best (config_019: multiprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool, weighted; acc=0.639) establishes that multiprofile + avgpool + weighted fusion is the strongest architecture. Among RNA encoders, pca_n2000 (0.639) far outperforms scgpt (0.525), but scvi_n200 remains completely untested in the multimodal multiprofile setting. Uncertainty: It is unclear whether a variational autoencoder (scvi), which learns a nonlinear latent representation of single-cell data, can match or exceed the linear PCA projection. scgpt's poor performance suggests learned encoders may struggle here, but scvi is architecturally distinct (VAE vs. generative transformer) and its behavior is genuinely unknown. What this tests: config_031 isolates the RNA encoder as the sole variable from the current best, directly measuring whether scvi_n200 can compete with pca_n2000 under the best-known aggregation/fusion regime. Why it is the best next experiment: It resolves the most important remaining design uncertainty (RNA encoder choice) with a single clean comparison, and the outcome will either confirm PCA as the optimal encoder (closing that search axis) or reveal a new promising direction—maximizing information gained per experiment under the limited budget."
}

